Hi [~accountid:60b0d240d435380069ba374b] 

In the agreement you shared - this one[https://docs.google.com/document/d/13EnZPRhfeKAeadhaaWhMZ2YOnF5eeIIh/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/13EnZPRhfeKAeadhaaWhMZ2YOnF5eeIIh/edit|smart-link]- there is no Annex 2 - DSA and section that the partner mentions. Can you please share the one that the partner has been working on to harmonise it as they mentioned? It should be another agreement as far as I see. 

Regarding their proposal /question: *I have commented about our approach to their proposal. I will reiterate it in this response :*

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
_To clarify our concerns, their proposed version is just a broad wording from the GDPR where we both are responsible for any damage to users. There is no need to put this into agreement as this is the requirement of the law and we are in any case liable even if the agreement does not specify this. Our clauses 9.2 and 9.3 of the Annex 2 to the General T&Cs, specify the liability of the parties in case this damage happened at fault by one of the Parties. Our version specifies that such parties are fully liable and any liability cap does not apply for privacy violations._
{panel}

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
_To sum up, the proposed ‘harmonisation’ by the vendor will remove very important clause regarding the liability and replace it with a very general wording from the GDPR._
{panel}

Hi, I looked at this a little bit deeper and found that this issue only seems to appear on endpoints which are defined as GET instead of POST.

Namely, this endpoint:

{noformat}adminPanelAuthRouter.get("/adminPanel/agentSkill/changelog/v2/getList", skillController.getChangelogV2);{noformat}

generates this API interface:

{noformat}export interface AgentSkillChangelogV2GetListRequest {
    agent_user_id: number;
    agent_user_type: AgentUserType;
}

export const AgentSkillChangelogV2GetListAgentUserType = {
        AdminUser: 'admin_user'
} as const;
export type AgentSkillChangelogV2GetListAgentUserType = typeof AgentSkillChangelogV2GetListAgentUserType[keyof typeof AgentSkillChangelogV2GetListAgentUserType];{noformat}

where {{AgentUserType}} is not found anywhere while {{AgentSkillChangelogV2GetListAgentUserType}} remains unused.



After I change the endpoint to:

{noformat}adminPanelAuthRouter.post("/adminPanel/agentSkill/changelog/v2/getList", skillController.getChangelogV2);{noformat}

this {{AgentSkillChangelogV2GetListRequest}} interface is no longer generated and instead the generated API looks like this:

{noformat}        public agentSkillChangelogV2GetList = async (body: GetChangelogRequest, opts?: TRequestOptions): Promise<ApiResponse<AgentSkillChangelogV2GetList200Response>>  => {
            return this.httpClient.sendRequest<ApiResponse<AgentSkillChangelogV2GetList200Response>>({
                 path: '/adminPanel/agentSkill/changelog/v2/getList',
                 service_id: 'beehive-agent',
                 http_method: HttpMethod.POST,
                 meta: {
                     auth: { enabled: true, strategy: AuthStrategy.JWT },
                     sharding: { enabled: false },
                     virtualPaths: { enabled: this.apiClientOptions?.virtualPathsEnabled ?? true }
                 },
                 body,
             }, opts);
         }


// in GetChangelogRequets.ts

export interface GetChangelogRequest {
    agent_user_id: number;
    agent_user_type: 'admin_user';
}{noformat}



We don’t really intentionally use {{GET}} method here, it’s just an older codebase where we forgot to use {{POST}}. Normally we try to avoid using {{GET}} and treat communication as RPC where {{POST}} is used across the board.

I will just migrate this endpoint to {{POST}} and therefore the above issue can be deprioritised (at least from our perspective).

