Hi [~accountid:641d5e830e6828ab20269e6d] 

I was approached with a request to review a Sales Enablement provider Outreach, which is currently used in Bolt Food for partners and now the teams plan to use it for Bolt Business.

I was made aware that you’ve reviewed the [MSA|https://drive.google.com/file/d/1XLbbPNkJ3FTZz3hnRjKksacHq5lp8uGy/view?usp=sharing] and approved the provider - [ticket|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-28158] back in 2024. *As I do not see any audit trail of the review, can I kindly clarify if you had any particular concerns with Outreach?*

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
Key point that I note is that we did not try to negotiate our own DPA template and instead agreed to the Outreach’s DPA (Addendum A).

*The default DPA itself looks fine to me, to summarise:*

# all basic requirements under Art. 28 covered;
# detailed but general enough description of the data transfer that could be extended to Bolt Business;
# correct UK&EU SCCs reference clauses inserted;
# detailed security measures and certifications;

*Main points of concern from my side:*

# Indemnity and LoL - overall, not beneficial for Bolt and no separate LoL under privacy clauses; MSA liability limited by 12 months worth of fees, which is this case would be 150K EUR I presume🔴 
# Irish DPC as the supervisory authority - not critical but we prefer AKI;
# Bolt’s audit rights limited to obtaining certification copies and reports annually.
# No timelines for data breach notifications, data subject requests
{panel}

